--TEST--
A property read through a union of classes is `E0881` when one class lacks the property or two classes give it different types — `rule:types/a-member-every-class-of-a-union-declares`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Box { public string $name = "boxed"; public function constructor() { } }
final class Circle { public int $size = 1; public function constructor() { } }
final class Label { public ?string $name = null; public function constructor() { } }

// `Circle` has no `$name`, so the read does not compile.
Box|Circle $either = new Box();
echo $either->name, "\n";

// Both classes have `$name`, but the types differ, so the read does not compile.
// The `??` after it reports nothing more.
Box|Label $titled = new Box();
echo $titled->name ?? "none", "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0881]: `Circle` has no property `$name`
  --> %s:8:6
  |
8 | echo $either->name, "\n";
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ used through `Box|Circle` here
  = help: you can use a member through a union only when every class has it with the same type, and it is visible here. Otherwise, test the value with `is` first

error[E0881]: `Box::$name` is `string`, and `Label::$name` is `string|null`, so the property has no one type
   --> %s:13:6
   |
13 | echo $titled->name ?? "none", "\n";
   |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ used through `Box|Label` here
   = help: you can use a member through a union only when every class has it with the same type, and it is visible here. Otherwise, test the value with `is` first

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
